# Controls the build context sent to the Docker daemon.
# Keep this small: a large context makes every build slow and can leak secrets.

# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Version control and virtualenv -----------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.venv
venv
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info

# --- Tooling caches ---------------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
htmlcov

# --- Kept, and why -----------------------------------------------------------
# README.md and pyproject.toml: the package metadata declares
# `readme = "README.md"`, so excluding it would break `pip install .` inside the
# image (COMMON_PITFALLS.md #6).
#
# migrations/: `researcher/storage/postgres.py` derives the repository root from
# its own `__file__` and applies the schema at startup. Excluding this directory
# still builds, and produces an image that dies on its first run against a
# database with `StorageError: migration directory not found`. It was excluded
# here until Phase 8 for the wrong reason: the host applies migrations too, so
# the omission was invisible until the container tried to.
#
# tests/, pytest.ini and requirements-dev.txt: the image runs the supplied smoke
# tests, which is how it is verified without spending provider quota. The
# Dockerfile installs the test subset of requirements-dev.txt and leaves the
# static-analysis tools to the host, where they belong.

# --- Not needed to build or run the image -----------------------------------
docs
report
slides
templates
artefacts
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
compose.yaml
